#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "How To Prepare Timeline"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:9
msgid "Define the goal"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:10
msgid "Before anything else: what should the site actually do? Sell a product, book appointments, publish articles, replace a broken WordPress install. One sentence is enough to start."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:11
msgid "You bring: the goal, the deadline, the budget range"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:14
msgid "Gather your materials"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:15
msgid "The single biggest cause of delay is missing content. Collect logo files, brand colours and fonts, photos, product data, legal pages and the text for each page — or tell me you need help writing it."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:16
msgid "You bring: logo, copy, images, 2–3 reference sites"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:19
msgid "Contact me or book a call"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:20
msgid "Send the brief by email or book a 20-minute call. I reply within a day with first questions and a rough feasibility answer — including an honest “this isn’t for me” when that’s the case."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:21
msgid "I deliver: reply in 24 h, first questions"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:24
msgid "Discuss ideas and agree the scope"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:25
msgid "We turn the brief into a written scope: page list, features, integrations, who writes the content, what is explicitly out of scope. You get a fixed quote or an hourly estimate with a cap, plus a timeline and payment schedule."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:26
msgid "I deliver: written scope, quote, timeline"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:29
msgid "Pick a direction — templates and design"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:30
msgid "You review layout templates and a design direction: typography, colour, section styles, and how it behaves on mobile. Choosing from a system is faster and cheaper than a blank-page design, and you can still customise every section."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:31
msgid "You bring: one round of consolidated feedback"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:34
msgid "Access and setup"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:35
msgid "Hosting, domain and DNS, repository, CMS accounts, analytics, payment or mailing providers. Send credentials through a password manager, never by email — and give me a staging environment rather than the live site."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:36
msgid "You bring: hosting, domain, CMS and analytics access"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:39
msgid "Build, with a demo you can watch"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:40
msgid "Development happens on a staging URL you can open any time. You get a short written update at each milestone, so nothing arrives as a surprise at the end."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:41
msgid "I deliver: staging link, milestone updates"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:44
msgid "Testing and the fix round"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:45
msgid "Cross-browser and real-device checks, Core Web Vitals, accessibility, forms, redirects and SEO metadata. You review on staging and send one consolidated list; I fix and re-test until it’s signed off."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:46
msgid "I deliver: test report, fixes, re-test"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:49
msgid "Launch, handover and aftercare"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:50
msgid "Go-live with backups and redirects in place, then you get the repository, all accounts in your name, a short walkthrough of how to edit content, and 30 days of bug cover. Optional monthly support continues from there."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/how-to-prepare-timeline.php:51
msgid "I deliver: launch, docs, ownership, 30-day cover"
msgstr ""

